<%#
  ONE OF THE PROJECT FOLDER'S DEPTH-ONE SUBFOLDERS, AS A PANEL (2026-09-08, folder panels; spec
  decisions 1, 3 and 6). Until now every subfolder was a <details> section inside the Files panel
  and the whole page shared ONE tiles/list cookie, so a maker could not have their models as tiles
  and their firmware checkout as the Finder browser. A folder is a first-class panel now: the
  page editor can hide it, move it and size it (projects/_panel_slot), and its VIEW is its own, persisted in
  `panels["views"]` under this panel's key.

  Locals: dir (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Dir), key ("folder:<node_id>"), view (one of
  Maker::Project::VIEWS). Reads @project, @generated_ids, @page_thumbs, @addon_origins and
  @repo_cards off ProjectsController#show, exactly as the section partial it replaces always did.

  NESTING IS UNCHANGED AND DELIBERATE: only DEPTH ONE is a panel, so a subfolder of a subfolder
  still renders through projects/_file_tree_section inside this panel, nested as it sits on disk.
  A repository at depth one is a panel like any other; one nested deeper stays a closed section
  with its browser inside it (spec decision 3).

  THE COUNT IS THE WHOLE SUBTREE, which is _file_tree_section's rule for a REPOSITORY applied to
  every folder here — and for the same reason: a panel holds its nested sections, so its heading
  must count what is inside them too, or a folder of folders reads "(0)". Generated files are
  subtracted for a plain folder because they render in the Files panel's Generated group instead
  and this panel really does not draw them; a repository's browser lists everything at every
  depth, so nothing is subtracted there (_file_tree_section makes the same split).

  ITS OWN `thumbs filemenu` PAIR. The Files panel wraps its groups in one instance because they
  share a subtree; a panel is a sibling subtree, so a controller mounted over there would not find
  these cells at all. Every tile id here is already in @page_thumbs: ProjectsController#show's union
  takes every listed file except those beneath a Dir its #dirs_without_tiles names, and those are
  exactly the files no panel draws a tile for (a hidden panel outside the editor, the browser view,
  a repository nested as a closed section) — so this polls, and never builds a second ThumbnailMap.
%>
<% visible = dir.files.reject { |row| @generated_ids.include?(row.node_id) } %>
<% count = dir.repo? ? dir.subtree_file_count : dir.subtree_file_ids.count { |id| !@generated_ids.include?(id) } %>
<% empty = visible.empty? && dir.children.empty? %>
<section class="panel folder-panel<%= " panel--quiet" if empty %>" id="<%= key %>">
  <div class="panel-head">
    <%# THE FOLDER'S OWN NAME IS THE DEFAULT, NOT THE TITLE (2026-09-09, the page editor): only this
        caller knows it — Layout holds node ids and PANEL_LABELS names no folder — so it is passed
        in, and the maker's own title wins over it when there is one. %>
    <h2><%= panel_title(@panel_layout, key, dir.name) %></h2>
    <span class="mono muted"><%= pluralize(count, "file") %></span>
    <%# WHERE IT IS, not just what: the subfolder's path, linked to it in the Library. The Files
        panel's own `panel-path` reads "Open folder →" since slice 6, with the path as its title —
        that folder is the page's own subject, where a subfolder's path is the news. %>
    <%= link_to dir.path, files_path(folder: dir.node_id), class: "panel-path mono muted" %>
    <% if dir.repo? %><span class="badge">repo</span><% end %>
    <div class="panel-actions">
      <% if dir.repo? %>
        <%= link_to "Commits", repo_commit_path(dir.node_id), class: "linkbtn" %>
        <%= link_to "History", repo_history_path(dir.node_id), class: "linkbtn" %>
      <% end %>
      <%# THREE BUTTONS, NOT LINKS, because this is a WRITE: the choice is persisted on the project
          row (Projects::PanelsController#update's `view` branch), not remembered in a cookie. Each
          posts `view[<key>]=<value>` and the door redirects back to this panel's own anchor.
          A SECOND COPY OF THIS MARKUP LIVES IN projects/_attachments.html.erb, offering two of the
          three: Files has no browser to mount (there is no Dir for the folder's own root unless it
          is a working tree), and a control that does nothing is worse than one that is absent. %>
      <div class="view-toggle" role="group" aria-label="View">
        <% Maker::ProjectKind.offered_views(key).each do |value| %>
          <%= button_to value.capitalize, project_panels_path(@project), method: :patch,
                        params: { view: { key => value } },
                        class: "toggle#{' active' if view == value}" %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%= panel_intro(@panel_layout, key) %>

  <% if empty %>
    <%# QUIET, NOT OMITTED (S4-1's quiet-panel rule). The maker put this folder in the layout — it
        is a real folder on disk — so the honest render is its heading and one sentence, the same
        answer an empty Tasks panel gives. Omitting it is the VISITOR's page's rule, not this one. %>
    <p class="muted">Empty folder.</p>
  <% else %>
    <div data-controller="thumbs filemenu" data-thumbs-url-value="<%= thumbnails_files_path %>">
      <%# THE CARD COMES FIRST IN EVERY VIEW — the README rendered, the latest commit, the current
          tag — which is the order _file_tree_section already puts it in for a nested repository.
          @repo_cards holds one for every repo? Dir on the page (ProjectsController#show), so a
          missing entry would be a real bug rather than a normal case; the `&&` is defensive. %>
      <% if dir.repo? && (card = @repo_cards[dir.node_id]) %>
        <%= render "projects/repo_card", card:, editable: false %>
      <% end %>
      <% if view == "browser" %>
        <%# THE FINDER-STYLE BROWSER (2026-09-07), which takes any Dir — a plain folder switched to
            this view browses exactly as a repository does, and it REPLACES the tiles, the rows and
            the nested sections rather than sitting above them. %>
        <%= render "projects/repo_browser", dir: %>
      <% else %>
        <% if visible.any? %>
          <% if view == "list" %>
            <%= render "file_rows", rows: visible %>
          <% else %>
            <div class="attachments-grid">
              <%= render partial: "file_tile", collection: visible, as: :row %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
        <%= render partial: "file_tree_section", collection: dir.children, as: :dir,
                   locals: { view: } %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</section>
